# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Design System

The single source of truth for {{PROJECT_NAME}} visual language, components, and design rules. Per-journey mocks (`docs/ux/jN.md`) and the components catalogue (`docs/ux/components.md`) reference this document; they do not redefine its tokens.

## 1. Principles

5-8 design principles. Examples to draw from:

1. **Restraint as discipline.** [Why this product needs restraint — kitchen reality / regulated context / cognitive load.]
2. **[Brand vibe in 4 words]** without [the cliché this product must avoid].
3. **[Primary device] reality.** [What the device imposes — touch, latency, reach, glance time.]
4. **Citations as trust mechanism.** Any AI-suggested value carries visible provenance; without citation there is no trust.
5. **[Regulatory or domain duty].** [What is non-negotiable.]
6. **[Spine metric].** What is the most weighted element on the screen and why.
7. **Agent-ready, agent-optional.** Same surfaces renderable by agents and humans; API is the contract.
8. **Boring before clever.** Reach for novelty only when convention fails the persona — and document why.

